# {{CLASS}} for FLEX

This starter provides a form field, a table column and an infolist entry. The field composes the existing FlexTextInput; its input HTML, CSS, JS, validation and state belong to that child. Column and entry share the package stylesheet and do not load the field JavaScript.

## Build and install

1. Set the package description and license in `composer.json`.
2. Run `composer install` with access to the FLEX Composer repository. Run `npm install`, then `npm run build`. Commit `package-lock.json`, `resources/asset-manifest.json` and the referenced `resources/dist/<release>` directory for distribution.
3. Install this package through Composer in a Laravel application. Its service provider is auto-discovered. Run `php artisan filament:assets` in that application.
4. Run `php artisan fff:assets:doctor` and `php artisan fff:assets:explain {{PREFIX}}-field`. The installation report explains dependencies; browser diagnostics separately show live owners and readiness.

When the build tools use FLEX from a different Composer installation, set `FLEX_FIELDS_ROOT` to that package directory. The build imports the public SDK facade; it refuses bundling private FLEX JavaScript. Build outputs are content-addressed. Failed compilation leaves the previous manifest intact. Previous release directories remain available; remove an unreferenced generation only when no installed release references it. No unrelated source directory is automatically deleted.

## Form

```php
use {{NAMESPACE}}\Forms\{{CLASS}}Field;

{{CLASS}}Field::make('summary')->required();
```

State is `['text' => 'Example']`. Store it in a JSON column with an Eloquent `array` cast. This starter does not authorize record access: use your resource policies and form validation. The nested container rejects unknown keys; the child validates text length.

## Configure the child directly

```php
use Bjanczak\FilamentFlexFields\Filament\Forms\Components\FlexTextInput;

{{CLASS}}Field::make('summary')->schema([
    FlexTextInput::make('text')
        ->label('Summary')
        ->required()
        ->maxLength(80),
]);
```

Reuse the actual public child class to configure its supported options. Additional children retain their own independent asset boundaries. A declared child slot describes composition and does not eagerly load its JavaScript.

## Table and infolist

```php
use {{NAMESPACE}}\Tables\{{CLASS}}Column;
use {{NAMESPACE}}\Infolists\{{CLASS}}Entry;

{{CLASS}}Column::make('summary');
{{CLASS}}Entry::make('summary');
```

Each cell and entry emits an independent consumer. Text is escaped by Blade. Adapt `DisplayValue` when changing your stored value shape.

## Extend the family

For readable development output, use `node build.mjs --development`. The default
`node build.mjs` produces minified production output. Both use the same public SDK
and manifest compiler. Distinct bytes produce distinct immutable release IDs;
publish the selected build instead of editing generated artifacts.

Declare additional surfaces with typed `ComponentDefinition` contracts. Use `stylesFrom` for CSS-only sharing, `uses` for full runtime composition, and `capabilities` for per-instance optional features. Keep dependencies in the Composer package that supplies them. If you add dynamic imports, esbuild and the manifest compiler capture those edges; workers, WASM and other opaque resource references need an explicit declaration. The field factory uses SDK-owned resources and disposes them in `destroy()`.


## Inspect registration and plan removal

The provider declares its registration source for every family surface. Source
paths remain server-side and appear only with an explicit operator option:

```shell
php artisan fff:assets:explain {{PREFIX}}-field --locations --json
php artisan fff:assets:doctor --definitions --locations --json
php artisan fff:components:removal {{PACKAGE}} --json
```

Removal inspection never uninstalls a package or deletes values. Inventory stored
schemas through `ComponentRemovalImpact` as well as the declared graph before
removing a package. Optional `RegistrationMetadata` can also declare a replacement
component, compatibility deadline and migration message using
`ComponentDeprecation`. Notices do not disable working components automatically.


## Appearance isolation

The generated shared CSS uses `--fff-ext-{{PREFIX}}--token-color` and
`--fff-ext-{{PREFIX}}--token-radius`, inheriting core appearance by default.
Override them through the request-scoped theme:

```php
use Bjanczak\FilamentFlexFields\Support\Theme\AppearanceNamespace;
use Bjanczak\FilamentFlexFields\Support\Theme\FlexFieldsTheme;

app(FlexFieldsTheme::class)->mergePackageTheme(
    new AppearanceNamespace('{{PREFIX}}'),
    ['color' => 'var(--fff-field-focus-border)', 'radius' => '0.75rem'],
);
```

Use `$package->appearance()` for font/keyframe names and owner-derived SVG IDs.
The same helpers are available through SDK ABI1 `createAppearanceNamespace()`.
Keep CSS selectors scoped to this package and reuse child renderers and their
asset boundaries. These helpers do not rewrite arbitrary CSS or download fonts.
